Performance Optimization
Q: How to optimize React performance?

Answer:

TSX
// 1️⃣ USE React.memo() for component memoization
const RestaurantCard = React.memo(({ restaurant }) => {
  // Only re-renders if 'restaurant' prop changes
  return <div>{restaurant.name}</div>;
});

// 2️⃣ USE useMemo() for expensive calculations
const expensiveValue = useMemo(() => {
  return someExpensiveCalculation(data);
}, [data]); // Only recalculate when 'data' changes

// 3️⃣ USE useCallback() for function memoization
const handleClick = useCallback(() => {
  // Function doesn't change reference unless dependencies change
  doSomething();
}, [dependency]);

// 4️⃣ CODE SPLITTING - lazy load components
const RestaurantDetail = lazy(() => import('./pages/RestaurantDetail'));

// 5️⃣ Virtual Lists - render only visible items
// For lists with 10,000+ items, use react-window

// 6️⃣ Avoid inline objects/arrays in props
// ❌ <Component data={{ id: 1 }} /> (new object every render)
// ✅ const data = { id: 1 }; <Component data={data} />
